<title>UK: Japanese aluminium stocks fell in 1996 - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Japanese aluminium stocks fell in 1996 - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Primary aluminium stocks in Japan fell in 1996, figures issued by the International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) show.</p>
<p>Inventories held by Japanese traders stood at 244,000 tonnes at the end of December 1996, down from the comparative December 1995 level of 273,000 tonnes. Japanese customer inventories dropped to 114,000 tonnes from 118,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The IPAI was issuing figures compiled by the Research and Statistics Department of Japan's Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI).</p>
<p>--London Newsroom 44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
